  "riskTitle": "Important: Risk of Data Loss",
  "riskSub": "The next steps will modify partitions or boot files on this disk. Read the full notice below, wait for the countdown, and check the confirmation box to continue.",
  "riskExpHead": "Experimental community port",
  "riskExpBody": "This Android build is an experimental community port and is not affiliated with or supported by Huawei, Qualcomm, or Google. No warranty is provided for your device or data, and hardware testing coverage is limited.",
  "riskDiskHead": "Disk changes are irreversible",
  "riskDiskBody": "The following operations modify the partition table or partition contents of the target disk. Software defects, storage faults, or unexpected power loss may corrupt or destroy your data. These changes cannot be undone, and lost data cannot be recovered by the installer.",
  "riskWipeHead": "Erase entire disk: all existing data will be erased",
  "riskWipeBody": "Every partition on the target disk — including Windows, personal files, other operating systems, and factory recovery partitions — will be permanently deleted. Restoring Windows afterwards will require a clean reinstallation from Windows installation media.",
  "riskAlongHead": "Keep existing system: partition table and boot files are still modified",
  "riskAlongBody": "Android will be installed into unallocated space without shrinking or deleting existing partitions, but the GPT partition table will still be updated and the boot manager (systemd-boot) will be installed to the shared EFI system partition. If an error occurs midway, your existing operating system may also fail to boot.",
  "riskReinstallHead": "Reinstall Android",
  "riskReinstallWipe": "Android system partitions will be rewritten and /data will be formatted: all installed apps, photos, messages, and other user data in Android will be permanently erased.",
  "riskReinstallKeep": "Android system partitions will be rewritten while keeping existing data on /data. However, downgrading to an older release or encountering an error during installation may still leave existing data unreadable; backing up beforehand is recommended.",
  "riskWinHead": "Windows and BitLocker recovery key",
  "riskWinBody": "Installation installs the boot manager (systemd-boot) to the shared EFI system partition and replaces the default boot file (BOOTAA64.EFI, with the original backed up). If BitLocker or Device Encryption is enabled in Windows, Windows may prompt for your 48-digit recovery key on its next boot; without that key, Windows and its files will be inaccessible. Before continuing, verify that you have access to your recovery key at https://aka.ms/myrecoverykey.",
  "riskWinBitlocker": "A BitLocker-encrypted volume was detected on this disk; you will be asked to confirm that you have your recovery key on the final confirmation page.",
  "riskEditHead": "Deleting partitions: their data becomes inaccessible immediately",
  "riskEditBody": "Proceed only after confirming what each partition contains: deleting the partition Windows is installed on will make Windows unbootable. The partition table is backed up to the installation medium before each deletion.",
  "riskBackupHead": "Back up important data to another device",
  "riskBackupBody": "Copy important files — such as photos, documents, Windows files, and Android app data — to another device, external storage, or cloud storage. Keeping copies on another partition of the same disk does not protect against disk-wide failure. If you have not backed up yet, click “Back”, shut down, and back up your data first.",
  "riskPowerHead": "Keep AC power connected throughout",
  "riskPowerBody": "Connect the power adapter before starting and keep it plugged in until the operation finishes. Power loss while writing to the disk will leave disk partitions in an incomplete state, preventing the system from booting or corrupting data. Do not hold the power button or force a restart while writing is in progress.",
  "riskNoCancelHead": "Cannot be cancelled once disk writes begin",
  "riskNoCancelInstall": "The next page is the final confirmation step. Once disk writes begin, the operation cannot be cancelled or rolled back (when downloading over the network, you may still cancel during the download stage before any changes are written to disk).",
  "riskNoCancelStep": "Each deletion on the next page takes effect immediately once confirmed; it cannot be interrupted midway or undone afterwards.",
